---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const effectiveDate = 'June 10, 2026';
const contactEmail = 'chad@chadfurman.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Build Aloud"
  description="How Build Aloud and its projects (including the Tower Defense game at td.buildaloud.ai) collect, use, and protect your data."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <span class="page-label">// privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="effective">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>
    </header>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect information across
      the <strong>buildaloud.ai</strong> property, including this blog and our projects
      hosted on subdomains — notably the <strong>Tower Defense</strong> game at
      <a href="https://td.buildaloud.ai">td.buildaloud.ai</a>. "We" refers to Build Aloud,
      operated by Chad Furman. Questions? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Usage &amp; device data.</strong> When you visit, we automatically receive
        standard technical data (browser type, device, pages viewed, and an IP address from
        which approximate location may be derived). This blog uses Google Analytics for
        aggregate usage statistics.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Account information (game).</strong> If you sign in to the Tower Defense
        game, we collect your email address. Sign-in uses Google Sign-In (OAuth) or a
        one-time "magic link" emailed to you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Game progress.</strong> The game stores your saved progress both locally on
        your device and, when you are signed in, in our cloud database so it syncs across
        devices.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Advertising data.</strong> The game shows ads via Google AdSense. Google and
        its partners may set cookies or similar identifiers to deliver ads and, where you
        consent, to personalize them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Post likes.</strong> To count a like once per device without an account, we keep
        a random device id in your browser — in both localStorage and a cookie — and, if you clear
        both, re-derive a similar id from your browser's characteristics (screen, timezone, language,
        and a Web Audio signal). That id is hashed on our server; we never store the raw
        characteristics, and it's device-level, not identity — we still don't know who you are.
        Separately, your IP is hashed with a secret salt only to rate-limit abuse, never to decide
        whether you've already liked. Under GDPR a device id and a salted IP hash are still personal
        data, so they're disclosed here even though neither reveals who you are. The honest tradeoff:
        clear your browser storage on a browser that also randomizes these signals (like Safari) and
        you can like a post again.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide, operate, and improve the blog and the game.</li>
      <li>To authenticate you and save and sync your game progress.</li>
      <li>To display advertising that helps keep the game free to play.</li>
      <li>To understand aggregate usage so we can make things better.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies &amp; similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      We and our service providers use cookies and similar technologies for analytics and,
      in the game, for advertising. If you are in the European Economic Area, the United
      Kingdom, or Switzerland, we ask for your consent before using non-essential cookies via
      a consent banner, and you can change or withdraw your choice at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>We rely on the following processors, each under its own privacy terms:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — authentication and storage of your game saves.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> — AdSense (ads), Analytics (usage), and Google Sign-In. See
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener" target="_blank">how Google uses data from sites that use its services</a>.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Resend</strong> — delivery of one-time sign-in emails.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Advertising &amp; your choices</h2>
    <p>
      Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on prior visits.
      You can opt out of personalized Google advertising via
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>,
      and out of many third-party vendors via
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>.
      In the EEA, UK, and Switzerland, advertising cookies are used only as permitted by your
      consent choice.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your account email and game saves while your account is active. You can request
      deletion of your account and associated data at any time by emailing
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or export
      your personal data, and to withdraw consent. To exercise any of these, email
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> and we will respond.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Our services are not directed to children under 13 (or under 16 in the EEA), and we do
      not knowingly collect personal data from them. If you believe a child has provided us
      data, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      We and our providers process data in the United States and other countries. By using
      our services you understand your information may be transferred and processed there.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as our services evolve. We will revise the "Effective" date
      above when we do; material changes will be noted on this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions or requests? Email <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 1.25rem 5rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .page-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .legal h1 {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0.4rem;
    font-size: 2.2rem;
  }

  .effective {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legal h2 {
    margin: 2.2rem 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal p,
  .legal li {
    color: var(--color-text, inherit);
  }

  .legal ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .legal li {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .legal a:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
</style>
